<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Oldenburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1774 CE – 1918 CE · capital Oldenburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">North German duchy, later grand duchy, created by a Danish-Russian exchange and ruled by a branch of the house that also held the Russian throne.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-oldenburg">County of Oldenburg</a> had been ruled by the Danish kings since 1667. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tsarskoye-selo-1773">Treaty of Tsarskoye Selo</a> of 1773, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> exchanged it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-holstein-gottorp">Gottorp</a> share of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a>, and Grand Duke Paul passed it to his relative <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-augustus-i-duke-of-oldenburg">Frederick Augustus</a>, prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-and-hanseatic-city-of-lubeck">Lübeck</a>. In 1774 the emperor raised Oldenburg to a duchy.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-holstein-gottorp">Holstein-Gottorp</a> line governed a Lutheran land of marshes, moors and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> farming, with the secularised <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-lubeck">Principality of Lübeck</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eutin">Eutin</a> and, from 1817, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-birkenfeld">Principality of Birkenfeld</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-i-grand-duke-of-oldenburg">Peter Frederick Louis</a> was a careful administrator. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> annexed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-oldenburg">Oldenburg</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1811, but it was restored in 1813 and became a grand duchy, adopting a constitution in 1849.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-oldenburg">Oldenburg</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-german-confederation">North German Confederation</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-augustus-ii-grand-duke-of-oldenburg">Grand Duke Frederick Augustus II</a> abdicated in November 1918, and the state became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-oldenburg">Free State of Oldenburg</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-oldenburg.jpg" alt="Duchy of Oldenburg" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Oldenburg_(Scandinavian_Cross).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1774 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Oldenburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Frederick Augustus I, Peter Frederick Louis, Frederick Augustus II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Grand Duchy of Oldenburg, Großherzogtum Oldenburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1846&amp;focus=duchy-of-oldenburg" aria-label="Duchy of Oldenburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4863 348 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Oldenburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5183 604L5183 604M5183 604L5054 728M5183 604L5199 691M5183 604L5300 622M5183 604L5183 604M5183 604L5165 704M5183 604L5235 577M5183 604L5176 592"/><path class="map-d